WEBVTT

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.500
"Meeting in progress"

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.630
"Together with Maman"
"New Segment Planning Meeting"

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.630
I think an education program
needs a handicraft segment.

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:16.510
"Together with Maman"
"New Segment Planning Meeting"

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:16.510
Yeah. I've been thinking that way, too.

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.720
And... an idea came to me.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:21.060
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.850
When insects build their nests,
they cut and paste leaves, right?

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:26.520
What? They do?

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:30.980
And I came up with an idea for
Iketeru Daga and Uramichi Omota

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.740
--Uh-huh, uh-huh.
--to become insects
and do simple papercraft.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.030
"Fun!!" "Great!!"

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.030
I see!

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:38.910
A parent and their child
can mimic it together, huh?

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:43.460
We'll have Utano-<i>chan </i>briskly
play the role of an instructor.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.420
Yeah. That suits her.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:49.340
She isn't the insect type.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:52.300
And their costume designs
would be like this.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:53.920
They look perfect!

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:26.060
"Life Lessons with Uramichi Oniisan"

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.600
"Crafting with Maman"

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.230
"Crafting with Maman"

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.230
Crafting with Maman!

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:32.020
"Episode 7: I Can Do It by Myself"
Kids!

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:35.110
"Episode 7: I Can Do It by Myself"
We'll do fun handicrafts together today!

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:36.400
Yay!

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.280
And we're going to make... this!

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:40.910
What's this?

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.410
Chains?

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:45.200
Also known as "shackles,"
which bind adults.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.540
Right. It's a necklace.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:50.170
Let's make necklaces together today!

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.290
We can make them?

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:52.880
How do we make them?

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:58.340
Before that, I'll call out my
dependable assistants who'll help us.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:00.550
Kamiteru-<i>kun</i>!

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:02.680
I'm right here!

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:05.930
"Kamiteru-<i>kun</i>
(Iketeru Oniisan)"

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:05.930
I'm Kamiteru-<i>kun</i>, a longhorn beetle.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:09.850
"Kamiteru-<i>kun</i>
(Iketeru Oniisan)"

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:09.850
I'm good at cutting things using scissors.

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:13.860
If allowed, I'd like to cut everything
in this world into pieces.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:17.190
But what's important is, I do it
within the bounds of the law.

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:21.030
If I cut this self-restraint and
rational mind into pieces,

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:24.450
that's when I'll go down.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:29.750
Now, I'll introduce you
to my other assistant.

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:31.580
Uramino-<i>kun</i>!

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.040
I'm right here!

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.670
"Uramino-<i>kun</i>
(Uramichi Oniisan)"

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.670
I'm Uramino-<i>kun</i>, a bagworm!

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:39.130
"Uramino-<i>kun</i>
(Uramichi Oniisan)"

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:39.130
I'm good at pasting things.

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:42.680
But I don't like it when others paste
labels on me. I hate being labeled!

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.010
Uramino-<i>kun</i>. Don't your legs feel cold?

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:46.890
They do!

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:51.350
If possible, I'd like to shut myself up
in a bag for the rest of my life.

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:52.520
--Okay, then!
--Hm?

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:56.360
I'll show you the materials we'll use.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:58.230
Origami paper and glue.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:01.400
Make sure you only use the scissors
with the help of an adult, okay?

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:05.570
First, cut a sheet of origami
into four narrow, long pieces.

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:07.490
Kamiteru-<i>kun</i>. Please show us how to do it.

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:08.660
Okay!

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:17.170
"Tremble, tremble, tremble, tremble..."

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:23.010
Hm?

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:27.640
Ah... Um... Maybe you got
a little nervous, Kamiteru-<i>kun</i>?

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:31.180
You cut it into pieces like this, okay?

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:32.930
Please try again!

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:35.480
Everyone makes mistakes.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:39.650
If it's a correctable mistake,
go ahead and fix it, okay?!

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:40.820
I'm sorry.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:42.740
"Tremble..."

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:45.740
"Tremble, tremble, tremble, tremble"

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:48.870
Hm?

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:52.450
"Help him!!"

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:52.450
Ah...

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:58.420
O-Ohh, so you must be having
some trouble using scissors, huh?

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:00.420
That's... right...

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:01.420
What?

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:05.380
Even though I can't read analog watches,

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:08.600
I was able to perform a scene
where I read an analog watch.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:10.390
Kamiteru-<i>kun</i>?

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:12.640
But I can't...

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:18.020
...play a longhorn beetle
perfectly anymore!

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:21.900
I can't cover up my inability
with my acting anymore!

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:24.190
Kamiteru-<i>kun</i>! Calm down!

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:26.490
This isn't a heavy role like that!

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:31.370
I can't... I can't play this role!

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:35.830
This isn't the time for your
elite acting standards to kick in.

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:39.460
When crouching down,
he totally looks like a roach.

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:40.920
Hey, Kumao-<i>kun</i>!

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:43.300
He needs mental care!

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:44.670
There, there, there...

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:47.130
"Rustle, rustle, rustle, rustle..."
Drink some water and take a deep breath.

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:50.970
"Rustle, rustle, rustle, rustle..."
You're doing okay. You're a fine
longhorn beetle right now.

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:54.020
"Rustle, rustle, rustle, rustle..."
Even longhorn beetles
have different personalities.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.730
"Rustle, rustle, rustle, rustle..."
So, you're fine.

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:57.350
"Rustle, rustle, rustle, rustle..."

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:01.940
"Rustle, rustle, rustle, rustle..."
The hiring rate for weirdos
in this program is really high.

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:06.280
Uramino-<i>kun</i>. What's wrong
with Kamiteru-<i>kun</i>?

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:08.240
Well...

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:12.200
An earnest, good person who can't
process the expectations of others well

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:16.410
sometimes gets crushed
by the pressure and loses it.

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:22.590
It's very possible that you kids
have rare latent talents within you.

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:27.340
But you can choose the path you
want to take on your own, okay?

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:31.890
People around you won't
stick with you forever.

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:35.520
No one can share in all the hard work
and agony you'll face.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:38.890
In the end, everyone is equally alone.

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.400
He's right, kids...

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:44.070
Don't try to live for someone else.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.320
Or you'll become like me.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:49.320
Who does Oneesan live for?

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:51.780
I'm not at liberty to say
anything about that.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.700
Hey, you all did a good job making those!

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:58.370
--Everyone in front of your TV!
Were you able to make them okay, too?

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:01.580
--Can you do it? Are you sure?
--Everyone in front of your TV!
Were you able to make them okay, too?

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:03.590
Okay, then go!

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:07.510
Kids, I'm sorry for getting worked up.

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:08.550
Are you okay?

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:10.800
It's okay to take your time
and rest, you know.

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:12.840
I'm sorry, Uramino-<i>kun</i>.

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:13.890
I...

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:15.760
Don't worry about it.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:17.390
Kamiteru-<i>kun</i>.

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:20.980
It's a good thing that you can do
things better than others, of course.

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:26.360
But sometimes, you can live
a relaxing life if you can't.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:27.860
Uramino-<i>kun</i>...

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:31.950
What in the world...

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:34.120
--Good work.
--Good work.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:40.160
Excuse me, but could you teach me
how you cut that paper from earlier?

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:41.580
--Sure.
--Hm?

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:43.580
Watch closely, okay?

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:46.040
You're deft, Iketeru-<i>kun</i>.
It'll be a piece of cake for you.

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:47.670
Be quiet.

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:49.210
What? Why?!

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:50.760
I can't focus.

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:00.680
So, how's your practice paying off?

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:03.060
Ah... I've managed...

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:04.810
...to be able to make at least this.

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:10.070
Whoa... His potential is incredible!

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:11.110
"Uramichi"

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:11.110
"To Uramichi Oniisan"

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:13.070
"Uramichi"
"To Uramichi Oniisan"

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:13.070
Uramichi Oniisan.

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:16.700
Hello, kids!

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:18.830
How are you?!

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:22.460
I'm Iketeru Oniisan.

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:25.130
I'm Utano Oneesan.

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:29.000
Iketeru Oniisan. What kind of
song should we sing today?

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:31.510
Hm?

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:37.970
Iketeru Oniisan?

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:40.970
What? Ah... U-Um...

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:44.310
Right. The first song is...

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:47.060
Um... Um...

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:49.940
The first session's shoot is complete!

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:51.740
We'll take a break now!

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:57.280
I wonder what's wrong with Iketeru-<i>kun</i>.

00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:59.620
How should I know?

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:01.410
Right.

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:04.500
Ow!

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:14.050
He seems preoccupied.

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:17.220
Being preoccupied is
a norm for him, though.

00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:20.350
Hm?

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:29.480
Iketeru Oniisan.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:33.530
Are you okay? Are you feeling
sick or something?

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:34.740
What?

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:38.780
Ahh... No, i-it's not like that at all.

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:39.870
Um...

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:42.740
Uramichi Oniisan...

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:46.210
What should I do?

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:48.920
I can't go home.

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:50.210
Hm?

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:53.420
The thing is...

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:55.340
"Last night"

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:58.640
"Last night"

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:58.640
One hundred funny
animal videos! Next up is...

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:01.850
"One Hundred
Funny Animal Videos"

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:01.850
...this cat who meows
with a strange voice!

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:07.600
What a strange voice, huh?

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:10.980
"Iketeru's older sister
Mabui Daga (32)"

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:12.730
"Iketeru's older sister
Mabui Daga (32)"

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:12.730
That's re-fa.

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:16.070
What? Isn't it do-fa?

00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:17.450
Huh?

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:20.030
It's re-fa, no matter how you look at it.

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:23.120
No. It's definitely do-fa.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:25.000
What? That's not possible.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.330
Are you stupid?

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:28.750
Those who call others stupid
are the stupid ones.

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:29.710
You're such a bonehead.

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:31.750
Bone--

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:32.670
You ding-dong.

00:10:32.670 --> 00:10:34.250
Dong...

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:37.880
I can't live with you.

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:39.220
What?

00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:42.510
Sayuri-<i>san</i>. The two of us will
live alone for a while, okay?

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:43.850
--Don't come home until
you stop being a ding-dong.

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:46.810
--Dong...
--Don't come home until
you stop being a ding-dong.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:49.310
Wait. Why?

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:50.770
That's re-fa.

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:52.980
No, it's do-fa.

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:55.110
Leave.

00:10:55.110 --> 00:11:00.410
So, I got into a huge
fight with my sister.

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:02.820
I don't know what to do now.

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:07.200
A fight over something like that?

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:08.410
Who cares which one it is?

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:09.580
--Are you guys children?
--What?

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:11.880
--Is that even a fight in the first place?
--Um...

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:15.710
He gets easily confused, so please
don't say things all at once like that.

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:22.550
Mabui-<i>chan </i>can be stubborn sometimes.

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:27.310
I've got an idea! If I remember correctly,
you're good friends with my sister, right?

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:31.020
What? Well, yeah. We went
to college together, so...

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:33.020
Then please take my sister!

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:34.980
See? He's already confused.

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:41.070
Please go out for dinner or something
and entice her to stay at your place!

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:45.780
Ahh, you meant that way. But I can't
because I live with my boyfriend.

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:46.830
Oh...

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:48.870
Then I'll look after your boyfriend!

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:50.080
Wait, wait, wait.

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:50.960
Let's make a trade!

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:53.420
Trade?! Don't make it more complex!

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:55.090
Then... Then...

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:58.300
How about he comes to my place,
and then, I go to Kumatani-<i>san</i>'s place?!

00:11:58.300 --> 00:11:59.840
It's getting more complicated.

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:01.220
That's fine with me, though.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:02.760
Kumao-<i>kun</i>, shut up.

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:03.890
Then... Um...

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:06.930
Fine. I'll kick my boyfriend out.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:08.470
Poor guy, that sucks for him.

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:10.480
Then why don't we all go
to Uramichi-<i>san</i>'s place?

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:11.480
What?

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:16.190
The kids for the second session
are coming in soon!

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:17.360
Okay!

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:18.480
Now, let's go.

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:20.150
Okay.

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:24.030
Hello, kids! How are you?!

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:26.780
I'm Uramichi Oniisan,
your gymnast Oniisan.

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:28.540
Let's be nice to each other
and play a lot again!

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:30.410
"Agggghhhh!"

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:30.410
Let's be nice to each other
and play a lot again!

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:35.960
--Mommy!
--Oh? What's going on?

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:38.500
You two aren't getting along, huh?

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:40.630
She hit me first!

00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:44.260
That's not true! He stepped on my foot!

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:47.390
Both of you might be half at fault.

00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:49.350
Let's apologize at the same time.

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:52.270
--No!
--I didn't do anything wrong!

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:54.140
Do you know why, not just me,

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:58.480
but many other adults can
get through the day to day?

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:02.690
It's because we've been apologizing
even when we're not at fault;

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:07.030
we're bound by "responsibility,"
which is a word like a spell.

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:09.160
Err...

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:13.870
But I definitely don't think an apology
means you're abandoning your pride...

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:17.040
...especially if you think
about your future social life.

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:19.290
Just like it gets harder

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:23.210
when you keep pressing the snooze
button because it's hard to get up,

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:26.550
that frustration is something
that gets amplified.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:29.300
So, there are things that can be easier
if you give yourself a push

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:31.260
and deal with it sooner.

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:32.850
Ah...

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:36.440
Um... I'm sorry that I hit you earlier.

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:39.980
Me, too. I'm sorry that
I stepped on your foot.

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:45.700
Yay! Both of you did great
by apologizing to each other!

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:49.620
But Uramichi-<i>san </i>uses the
snooze button a lot, doesn't he?

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:00.750
I... I'm home.

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:03.170
"Illustrated Guide to the Ocean"
"The Ecology of the Spotted Garden Eel"

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:07.380
Um... Sis...

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:10.390
I'm sorry about yesterday. I...

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:12.060
Ahh...

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:14.020
Welcome back.

00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:16.520
"About yesterday"?

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:18.020
What're you talking about?

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:24.900
What was it about?

